### Has Key Primitive

The has key primitive will set the value of a participant or a key of a participant.

```text
hasKey <source> <key> <target> [keys]
```
Syntax Structure:
- `Set`:
    * Type: *string*
    * This is the identifier for the instruction.
- `<source>` 
    * Type: *string*
    * This is the name of the participant that will be evaluated.
- `<target>` 
    * Type: *string*
    * This is the name of the participant that will be written to.
- `[keys]` 
    * Type: *Array*
    * This is an array of strings, representing the key path to the target to set. 
    * For example, ["a","b"] will be target_participant["a"]["b"]
    * If the key is specified as [], it indicates that the value should be directly assigned to the participant.

#### Example 1:
Checks if a participant has a key specified by a participant.

```text
create has_name
hasKey book keyName has_name []
```

Pre-transformation state:
```text
    {
        book: {"name": "Lord of the Rings"},
        keyName: "name",
    }
```

Post-transformation state:
```text
    {
        has_name: true,
    }
```